order-top:solid #000000 0.5pt;vertical-align:top;padding:5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.7999999999999998;text-align: justify;margin-top:10pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><font face=\"Georgia\">Communication<\/font><\/span><\/p><\/td><td style=\"border-left:solid #000000 0.5pt;border-right:solid #000000 0.5pt;border-bottom:solid #000000 0.5pt;border-top:solid #000000 0.5pt;vertical-align:top;padding:5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.7999999999999998;text-align: justify;margin-top:10pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><font face=\"Georgia\">Students explain project logic<\/font><\/span><\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr style=\"height:25pt\"><td style=\"border-left:solid #000000 0.5pt;border-right:solid #000000 0.5pt;border-bottom:solid #000000 0.5pt;border-top:solid #000000 0.5pt;vertical-align:top;padding:5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.7999999999999998;text-align: justify;margin-top:10pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><font face=\"Georgia\">Teamwork<\/font><\/span><\/p><\/td><td style=\"border-left:solid #000000 0.5pt;border-right:solid #000000 0.5pt;border-bottom:solid #000000 0.5pt;border-top:solid #000000 0.5pt;vertical-align:top;padding:5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.7999999999999998;text-align: justify;margin-top:10pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><font face=\"Georgia\">Group projects encourage collaboration<\/font><\/span><\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><font face=\"Georgia\">Schools are now shifting from \u201ccomputer periods\u201d to technology-led learning experiences.<\/font><\/span><\/p><h3 style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; margin-top: 18pt; margin-bottom: 6pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><font face=\"Georgia\" style=\"\">How Coding Is Introduced in Primary Classes<\/font><\/span><\/h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 12pt;\"><font face=\"Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\">An <\/span><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\">English Medium School in Lucknow<\/span><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"> usually begins coding exposure through visual learning instead of complicated programming languages. Younger children learn through games, drag-and-drop activities, puzzles and storytelling exercises. The goal is not to create software engineers in Class 2. The goal is to develop curiosity.<\/span><\/font><\/p><h3 dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; margin-top: 16pt; margin-bottom: 4pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"><font face=\"Georgia\">Common methods used in primary grades<\/font><\/span><\/h3><ul style=\"font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; padding-inline-start: 48px;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 12pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.7999999999999998;margin-top:12pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><font face=\"Georgia\">Block-based coding platforms<\/font><\/span><\/p><\/li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 12pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.7999999999999998;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><font face=\"Georgia\">Story-building games<\/font><\/span><\/p><\/li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 12pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.7999999999999998;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><font face=\"Georgia\">Animation creation activities<\/font><\/span><\/p><\/li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type: disc; font-size: 12pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;\" aria-level=\"1\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.7999999999999998;margin-top:0pt;margin-botto